   $q$In sentence (7), the writer begins with "However" in order to:$q$, $q$[{"text":"indicate that the writer now agrees with the coaches.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"reverses-meaning"},{"text":"signal a response to the coaches' objection in sentence (6).","is_correct":true},{"text":"show that sentence (7) is an example of the objection in sentence (6).","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contrast-as-example"},{"text":"introduce a second opposing view from a different group of coaches.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-transition"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$signal a response to the coaches' objection in sentence (6).$q$, $q$"However" marks a turn from the coaches' worry about cancellations to the writer's answer that the system adjusts practices rather than ending them. The writer does not agree with the coaches; sentence (7) disputes their prediction.$q$, 'draft', '7f0cd155-6a0b-5ba4-a5c4-57de51c0cd9a')
