  ('6813c233-263e-5357-a898-5df9d7ddc027', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g12-argument-writing'), null, 'medium',
   $q$Which sentence, added after sentence (3), best explains how that evidence supports the claim?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Some schools in other states have already switched to newer measuring tools.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"new-evidence-not-reasoning"},{"text":"Humidity is the amount of water vapor present in the air at a given time.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"definition-not-reasoning"},{"text":"Under the current rule, practice would continue on the more dangerous of those two afternoons and be canceled on the safer one.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Many athletes feel tired and thirsty during long practices in late summer.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"vague-support"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Under the current rule, practice would continue on the more dangerous of those two afternoons and be canceled on the safer one.$q$, $q$The correct sentence links the fact in sentence (3) to the flaw in the current rule, showing why a better measurement is needed. The sentence about other schools adds a new fact but does not explain the evidence already given.$q$, 'draft', '7f0cd155-6a0b-5ba4-a5c4-57de51c0cd9a')
