insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('242328e9-3dd5-568d-a0d2-763fe7f08981', 'wg12-argument-writing-p05', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g12-argument-writing'), null,
        '9-12', $q$Keeping the Darkroom at Linden Hall$q$, $q$(1) Linden Hall's art department has proposed converting the school's film darkroom into a storage closet, arguing that digital cameras have made it obsolete. (2) The darkroom should be repaired and kept, because it teaches lessons about light, chemistry and patience that a digital screen cannot. (3) In a darkroom, students must calculate exposure times and mix developer at precise temperatures, which turns abstract ideas from physics and chemistry class into visible results. (4) Each print takes many minutes, so students learn to plan an image carefully instead of taking two hundred shots and hoping one works. (5) Last spring, 46 students signed up for the darkroom elective, more than for any other art course.

(6) The art department's concerns are not unreasonable. (7) Repairing the ventilation fan and the enlarger would cost roughly 2,400 dollars, and the chemicals require careful handling and disposal. (8) A local photography club has offered to donate a used enlarger, and the district's science supply contract already includes safe chemical disposal for the chemistry labs. (9) The storage the department needs could go in an unused classroom on the third floor.

(10) Digital photography is great too, and phones take really good pictures nowadays.$q$, 'draft')
