  ('b3c33805-ceca-5ca9-9e91-fc0168084592', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g12-argument-writing'), null, 'medium',
   $q$Which detail, added after sentence (3), would best support the point that sentence makes?$q$, $q$[{"text":"During a joint lesson last year, students compared development times at two temperatures and graphed how warmer developer darkened their prints.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Several students said the darkroom's red light gives the room a calm, relaxing atmosphere.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"off-point-evidence"},{"text":"The darkroom was built in 1971, when film was the only option for school photographers.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"irrelevant-detail"},{"text":"Film cameras can often be bought secondhand for much less than new digital ones.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"supports-other-point"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$During a joint lesson last year, students compared development times at two temperatures and graphed how warmer developer darkened their prints.$q$, $q$Sentence (3) says darkroom work turns science concepts into visible results, and graphing development times at different temperatures is a concrete example of that. The comment about the calm atmosphere is about mood, not about learning science.$q$, 'draft', '242328e9-3dd5-568d-a0d2-763fe7f08981')
