  ('fa2131fc-e07b-5829-bf00-3d967dd5eb41', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g12-argument-writing'), null, 'hard',
   $q$Sentence (9) answers a concern the writer never states. Which sentence, added after sentence (6), would best set up sentence (9)?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The vendors at Saltmarsh have sold food there for many years and know their customers well.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"irrelevant-detail"},{"text":"Many shoppers, however, say they would gladly pay a small deposit to reduce trash.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"evidence-not-concern"},{"text":"They also worry that reusable containers may cost more to buy at the start of the program.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"mismatched-concern"},{"text":"They also worry that collecting and washing containers would pull them away from serving customers.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$They also worry that collecting and washing containers would pull them away from serving customers.$q$, $q$Sentence (9) explains that a paid crew would do the washing so vendors keep their time, which answers a concern about labor at the stalls. The concern about purchase cost is reasonable but is not the one sentence (9) responds to.$q$, 'draft', 'd492cdf2-cc0f-59be-b2e6-16301d408b35')
