   $q$Which sentence would best replace sentence (10) as a conclusion that follows from the argument?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The market should ban all disposable containers next season and fine vendors who use them.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-reasoning"},{"text":"Reducing waste is everyone's responsibility, at home, at school and at work.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-general"},{"text":"Greyfield's results suggest a deposit system could cut Saltmarsh's largest source of trash without costing vendors sales or time.","is_correct":true},{"text":"The market should also add more benches and shade so shoppers stay longer.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"introduces-new-topic"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Greyfield's results suggest a deposit system could cut Saltmarsh's largest source of trash without costing vendors sales or time.$q$, $q$The correct conclusion restates the claim and answers both vendor concerns using the evidence from Greyfield. A ban with fines goes beyond the voluntary deposit system the essay argued for and ignores the vendors' worries.$q$, 'draft', 'd492cdf2-cc0f-59be-b2e6-16301d408b35')
