   $q$Why does the comparison in sentence (4) strengthen the argument?$q$, $q$[{"text":"It proves that wash stations will keep every lake in the state free of mussels forever.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"overgeneralizes"},{"text":"It suggests the wash station, not luck, kept Pinecrest clean, since nearby lakes without one became infested.","is_correct":true},{"text":"It shows that Pinecrest Reservoir is larger and more popular than Lake Tarrow.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"It explains why mussel larvae are too small to see during an inspection.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-function"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$It suggests the wash station, not luck, kept Pinecrest clean, since nearby lakes without one became infested.$q$, $q$Pairing Pinecrest with nearby unprotected lakes over the same period makes the wash station the likely reason for the difference. The comparison supports the claim but does not prove a permanent result for every lake.$q$, 'draft', '4f0cc545-43a3-5140-89ca-2f194f58e4a4')
