   $q$The writer wants to add a sentence after sentence (9) to complete the response to the anglers. Which choice is best?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Anglers who complain about a short wait are not thinking about the future of the lake.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"dismissive-tone"},{"text":"Fishing is a popular pastime that brings many visitors to the region every summer.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"off-point"},{"text":"Pinecrest also sells fishing licenses at its wash station for the convenience of visitors.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"irrelevant-detail"},{"text":"A delay that short, with the station open before sunrise, is unlikely to cost anglers the early hours they value.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$A delay that short, with the station open before sunrise, is unlikely to cost anglers the early hours they value.$q$, $q$The correct choice explains how the evidence in sentences (8) and (9) answers the anglers' specific concern about early launches. Blaming anglers dismisses the objection that sentence (7) said deserved an answer.$q$, 'draft', '4f0cc545-43a3-5140-89ca-2f194f58e4a4')
