   $q$Which sentence, added after sentence (1), would best show that the threat to Lake Tarrow is urgent rather than merely possible?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Last summer, boats that had recently been in two of those infested lakes were logged at Tarrow's public launch more than 300 times.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Some experts believe mussels could someday spread to lakes across the region.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"hedged-evidence"},{"text":"Lake Tarrow is known for its clear water and excellent trout fishing.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"irrelevant-detail"},{"text":"Invasive species have been studied by biologists for well over a century.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-general"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Last summer, boats that had recently been in two of those infested lakes were logged at Tarrow's public launch more than 300 times.$q$, $q$Hundreds of recorded visits from infested lakes show that mussels are already arriving at the launch, which makes the risk immediate. The expert prediction is about what could happen someday, so it makes the threat sound less urgent, not more.$q$, 'draft', '4f0cc545-43a3-5140-89ca-2f194f58e4a4')
